[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi all! <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"747491\">@Zichen Wang</span>  and I have formalized the following two theorems and  opened a PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38551\">#38551</a>to mathlib:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan_prod_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior_prod_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddTorsor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The first one says the affine span of a product set is the product of the affine spans, and the second is the affine analogue of <code>interior_prod_eq</code> for the intrinsic interior. Feedback is very welcome!</p>",
        "id": 590978236,
        "sender_full_name": "Yifan Bai",
        "timestamp": 1777217016
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>About affineSpan_prod_eq, I was thinking whether there should be a series of analog lemma through Submodule.span -&gt; vectorSpan -&gt; affineSpan. Then I learned for Submodule there is only an inequality version <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Span/Basic.html#Submodule.span_prod_le\">Submodule.span_prod_le</a>. Is the equality not true for submodules?</p>",
        "id": 590979498,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1777218009
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And secondly, does it make sense to define <code>AffineSubspace.prod</code> similar to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Span/Basic.html#Submodule.prod\">Submodule.prod</a> ? So that the equality is promoted from Set equality to AffineSubspace equality</p>",
        "id": 590979627,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1777218117
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think for the Submodule version to be true, both s and t needs to have the zero vector. I wonder if this is still simpler to prove for Submodule first, and you can transfer the result to affine space with fewer lines</p>",
        "id": 590981059,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1777219265
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I got Aristotle to prove the submodule version, and it is not very long. You should be able to get this to vectorSpan, then affineSpan. The total line count might increase, but it will be mostly boiler plates for writing lemma doc and signatures, and the actual proof for each lemma should be short</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>Submodule.span_prod_eq</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>theorem Submodule.span_prod_eq {R : Type*} {M : Type*} [Semiring R] [AddCommMonoid M] [Module R M] {M&#39; : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M&#39;] [Module R M&#39;] (s : Set M) (t : Set M&#39;) (hs : 0 ∈ s) (ht : 0 ∈ t) :\n    span R (s ×ˢ t) = (span R s).prod (span R t) := by\n  refine&#39; le_antisymm _ _;\n  · exact span_prod_le s t;\n  · rw [ Submodule.prod_le_iff ];\n    constructor &lt;;&gt; rw [ map_span ];\n    · rw [ span_le ];\n      rintro _ ⟨ x, hx, rfl ⟩;\n      exact Submodule.subset_span ( Set.mk_mem_prod hx ht );\n    · exact Submodule.span_mono ( Set.image_subset_iff.mpr fun x hx =&gt; ⟨ hs, hx ⟩ )\n</code></pre></div>\n\n</div></div>",
        "id": 590983308,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1777221081
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you for the helpful suggestions! Going through <code>Submodule.span</code> → <code>vectorSpan</code> → <code>affineSpan</code> sounds like a great approach, and I'm working on it. I'll update the PR once it's ready.</p>",
        "id": 591038268,
        "sender_full_name": "Yifan Bai",
        "timestamp": 1777263946
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Update: We've added a few more theorems along the way and refactored the proof of <code>affineSpan_prod_eq</code> to go through <code>Submodule.span</code> → <code>vectorSpan</code> →  <code>affineSpan</code>, as suggested. The full list is:</p>\n<p>In <code>Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Prod.lean</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">span_prod_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In <code>Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/AffineSpace/AffineSubspace/Basic.lean</code>, we added the <code>AffineSubspace.prod</code> construction</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AffineSubspace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AffineSubspace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AffineSubspace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">AffineSubspace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">carrier</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">smul_vsub_vadd_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp₃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">smul_vsub_vadd_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp₁</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp₂</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp₃</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">smul_vsub_vadd_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp₁</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp₂</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp₃</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>together with its basic API (<code>prod_coe</code>, <code>mem_prod</code>, <code>prod_mono</code>, <code>prod_top</code>, <code>prod_bot</code>, <code>prod_inf_prod</code>), and then:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AffineSubspace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">vectorSpan_prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">vectorSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">vectorSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">vectorSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AffineSubspace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan_prod_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AffineSubspace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan_prod_set_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">affineSpan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In <code>Mathlib/Analysis/Convex/Intrinsic.lean</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior_prod_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>We're not sure these are all in the most appropriate locations — in particular, we introduced a new <code>Prod</code> section in <code>AffineSubspace/Basic.lean</code> for the <code>AffineSubspace.prod</code> API, but it might fit better elsewhere.</p>",
        "id": 591069061,
        "sender_full_name": "Yifan Bai",
        "timestamp": 1777277575
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The set version of affineSpan prod can use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=spanPoints#doc\">docs#spanPoints</a></p>",
        "id": 591110126,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1777289589
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>spanPoints</code> should be considered an internal implementation detail, not something to be used outside of the definition of <code>affineSpan</code>. (There's also an argument for redefining <code>affineSpan</code> as an infimum, so <code>affineSpan_eq_sInf</code> becomes the result true by defeq and <code>mem_affineSpan_iff_exists</code> becomes the result with a non-defeq proof, but whether or not that is done, direct use of <code>spanPoints</code> should still be avoided.)</p>",
        "id": 591260467,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Myers",
        "timestamp": 1777337355
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If that's the case, should we remove the <code>@[simp]</code> tag from <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=coe_affineSpan#doc\">docs#coe_affineSpan</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 591264557,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1777340205
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I personally don't understand why <code>spanPoints</code> exists at all/is public</p>",
        "id": 591300403,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777361656
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The existence is because I originally set up the affine span in terms of <code>Submodule.span</code>, so using that definition along the way to defining <code>affineSpan</code>. I think it should definitely be private (and so not <code>simp</code>-normal for anything), and arguably shouldn't exist if the affine span is redefined as an infimum (with <code>mem_affineSpan_iff_exists</code> remaining as a lemma to state the relation to <code>vectorSpan</code> and thus to <code>Submodule.span</code>, rather than being true by definition any more). As far as I know, since <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/23255\">#23255</a> all <code>spanPoints</code> lemmas have had equivalent <code>affineSpan</code> versions.</p>",
        "id": 591599431,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Myers",
        "timestamp": 1777412516
    }
]